.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payments-redrive - Re-send a signed transaction whose broadcast never reached the chain (payee)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payments redrive   [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Ask the gateway to broadcast again a transaction that was prepared and SIGNED
but never reached the chain — a worker that died between the two, a drained queue.
The same signed bytes go out again; nothing about the payment changes, and no new
signature is asked for.

.PP
Only a transaction reading 'redrivable: true' qualifies (see 'payments
transaction' or 'payments transactions'). A pending row WITHOUT a signed
transaction is not stuck, it is unfinished: re-run the operation instead. The
gateway also redrives on its own recovery cadence; this asks for it now.

.PP
When the gateway's job queue is unreachable the redrive is refused with 503
queue_unavailable: nothing was enqueued and the transaction is unchanged, so
retry later.

.PP
Payee only. Add -w/--wait to block until the transaction confirms (or fails).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for redrive

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=15m0s
	Max time to wait when --wait is set; unset, 10× the chain's measured p90 settlement, kept within 5m–15m

.PP
\fB-w\fP, \fB--wait\fP[=false]
	Block until the operation confirms on-chain (or fails)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payments redrive 0xabc123… 7f1c0c8e-… --wait
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payments(1)\fP
